<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambulocetus-natans-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Ambulocetus natans Turing wavenumber at 224 µm (47.5 Ma, detail primordium) — Model fidelity to source: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The script integrates the Schnakenberg system and the Turing dispersion eigenvalue. Onset k_c and the fastest-mode k are both computed and are not treated as the same number. Gamma rescales time only. The integer Lean file pins the trace-diffusion sign and the 190 < 224 < 260 µm order." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambulocetus-natans-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambulocetus-natans-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambulocetus-natans-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambulocetus-natans-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Ambulocetus natans Turing wavenumber at 224 µm (47.5 Ma, detail primordium) — Morphometric validation: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Analytic versus Euler growth rates give Pearson r=0.9997 and RMSE=0.0034. The nonlinear radial peak is about 178 µm against the 224 µm slot target. Otsu foreground fraction, structure-tensor coherency and a KS test compare the fossil photograph with the field, and those pairs are not value==reference." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambulocetus-natans-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-dispersion-pearson-r-analytic-eigenvalue-vs-forward-euler>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambulocetus-natans-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-dispersion-rmse>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambulocetus-natans-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-emergent-stripe-wavelength>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambulocetus-natans-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-equal-diffusion-ablation-final-activator-std>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambulocetus-natans-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-image-foreground-fraction>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambulocetus-natans-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-image-structure-tensor-coherency>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambulocetus-natans-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-image-vs-model-orientation-ks-statistic>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambulocetus-natans-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambulocetus-natans-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambulocetus-natans-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Ambulocetus natans Turing wavenumber at 224 µm (47.5 Ma, detail primordium) — MorphoEval overall 87.3/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 implements Schnakenberg kinetics at a=0.05, b=0.90, Du=1, Dv=50, with the physical length chosen so the fastest analytic mode is 224 µm. Forward-Euler mode growth matches the eigenvalue curve at Pearson r=0.9997 (RMSE=0.0034). The nonlinear field on a 50x50 periodic patch selects about 178 µm, short of the 224 µm target, which is reported rather than forced. Equal diffusion is stable. The GIF (12 frames, 720x540) paints that field into a flank window of the Naturalis mount (Ghedoghedo, CC BY-SA 3.0). Hydration factors for Pakicetus (0.72) and Rodhocetus (1.35) are a transfer hypothesis, not fossil measurements. ANALYSIS_PASS is still 1. Overall 87.3/100 (faithfulness 86.3, reproducibility 89.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit dff4f2b5; environment: python 3.12, numpy 2.5, scipy 1.18. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 82, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/ambulocetus_natans_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-ambulocetus-natans-turing-wavelength-s0.py at dff4f2b5, image/gif, 3240023 B, 720×540 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 d0ad8d52ca0864aef0caa8c4b9c414223694d9ddb756c1c6966ad822630261d7 (sha256 d0ad8d52ca0864aef0caa8c4b9c414223694d9ddb756c1c6966ad822630261d7), spec_fingerprint 82d5550289ea52c71a2cf9496547413e4cf4267d76c981bb4448f33443a3774d. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 82d5550289ea52c71a2cf9496547413e4cf4267d76c981bb4448f33443a3774d; artifact_sha256: d0ad8d52ca0864aef0caa8c4b9c414223694d9ddb756c1c6966ad822630261d7; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/ambulocetus_natans_turing_wavelength_s0/ambulocetus_natans_naturalis_specimen.jpg=738e2188c8bb2936..., datasets/ambulocetus_natans_turing_wavelength_s0/ambulocetus_natans_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=0246234fefb8db6a...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability at a finite wavenumber. | Schnakenberg 1979: activator-inhibitor kinetics du/dt = a - u + u^2 v + Du lap u. | Thewissen, Hussain and Arif 1994: Ambulocetus natans, amphibious archaeocete, early middle Eocene of Pakistan. | Thewissen et al. 2001 and Gingerich et al. 1994: Pakicetus is more terrestrial; Rodhocetus is more aquatic.; reconstructed_in_script: Dimensionless parameters a=0.05, b=0.90, Du=1, Dv=50 and gamma=8, length-scaled to a 224 µm fastest mode. | Forward-Euler dispersion check and a nonlinear periodic patch. | Chronoseries wavelengths 190, 224 and 260 µm from lambda = 224 µm * sqrt(h).; transfer_boundary: Hydration h=0.72 and h=1.35 are this slot's reconstruction of how dermal diffusivity could change from Pakicetus to Rodhocetus. They are not in the fossil papers. | The flank window is a visualization of a dermal primordium on a photograph of bone.; does_not_claim: That 224 µm stripes are preserved on the Naturalis skeleton. | That the emergent 178 µm peak was measured on a fossil skin.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'ANALYSIS_PASS is 1, so extra seeds are skipped and no cross-seed wavelength CV is reported.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Specimen segmentation is global Otsu. Largest-component cleanup is gated off, so dark-background specks can enter the mask.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Pakicetus and Rodhocetus wavelengths are analytic sqrt(h) only. The nonlinear patch is not re-run at h=0.72 and h=1.35.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.73e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambulocetus-natans-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Ambulocetus natans Turing wavenumber at 224 µm (47.5 Ma, detail primordium) — Parameter expressivity: 82/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Hydration h moves the analytic wavelength as sqrt(h), and the bar chart shows Pakicetus < Ambulocetus < Rodhocetus. Equal diffusion flips the sign of the maximum growth rate. Pass 1 does not yet re-simulate the nonlinear patch at the predecessor and successor hydrations." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
