    dct:description "The comparison figure places the Naturalis mount beside the simulated field and the last GIF frame. The mount is recognizable. The dermal pattern is an inset, not a claim that the bones are striped. Soft-tissue pigment is absent from the fossil, so this cannot be a pigment-photograph match." ;
